summary: check if PSI featrue works
description: |
    Linux Kernel 4.20 includes PSI metrics (pressure stall information) for CPU, memory, and IO.
    PSI provides for the first time metrics for resources.
    Both the kernel and cgroup2 include pressure metrics.

    This case will run stress-ng to generate stress of resources, and check if statistics of PSI increses.
    Then move stressful process to Cgroup v2 subsystem, check if PSI works in Cgroup v2.
    For trigger registered, the case would generate stress in the same group that trigger in.
contact: Chunyu Hu <chuhu@redhat.com>
test: bash ./runtest.sh
framework: beakerlib
require:
  - gcc
  - glibc
recommend: []
duration: 90m
extra-summary: /kernel/general/schedular/sched_psi
extra-task: /kernel/general/schedular/sched_psi
